# Personnel Excel catalog import

Status: DISPATCH_READY
docType: work_order
dispatchKind: INITIAL
Risk: R2
Date: 2026-11-08
Commit owner: Root

## Dispatch Prompt Envelope

Read this exact packet, locked SPEC/ADR, current canonical continuity and its action assessment before code. Implement the PNI milestone E1-E6: a selected additive flat-XLSX people import with inspect/preview/confirm/cancel, existing-owner preservation and actual packaged Windows consumer proof. Terra owns server/catalog/UI integration; Sol owns reader/dependencies/offline builder and native verification; Astra is independent REVIEWER. Root alone owns authority, continuity, receipts and commits. No worker may commit or dispatch another worker. This packet takes effect only after independent exact-action acceptance and a fresh successful pre-dispatch; DISPATCH_READY alone is not admission.

## Authority, outcome and scope

Authority is the operator's 2026-11-08 instruction to audit and proceed with the stated reviewer/workers, the audited first-slice roadmap `docs/roadmaps/TAN_THUAN_PORT_ADOPTION.md`, `docs/specs/PERSONNEL_EXCEL_IMPORT.md` and `docs/decisions/ADR_PERSONNEL_EXCEL_READER.md`. Inherit DESIGN decisions and enter SPEC/WORK_ORDER at their earliest open stage; do not reopen settled CRC recovery or silently adopt the later E7 scope. Native project owners already provide catalog validation, context/digest, backup, people selection and report persistence; implement only the missing import connection and bounded additive safety operation. Release candidate version is1.9.2; the original D2 version was tentative and its separate work is not implemented by this order.

Required useful result: in a disposable Windows consumer flow the user selects a supported personnel workbook, sees exact row effects/errors and fields retained, confirms selected names, uses a newly added person in a report, exits/reopens and exports with old reports unchanged. No automatic team assignment, identity migration, inferred department, multi-department expansion or cross-project synchronization. Generic manually selected flat lists need no declaration that the inspected template is the unit's canonical live roster.

